§§ `ד. הוראות מעבר — שכר מנהלים קיימים`

-- §40(א): the "determining day" is 1.3.2014. (ב): an "existing principal",
-- academic or not, held his post in the school or institution on its eve.
@ref akn:art_40__para_a akn:art_40__para_b
GIVEN `appointed on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing principal of 2015` `appointed on` IF
    `in post on the eve of the determining day` `appointed on`

-- §41: chapter ד is for existing principals. §42: they are paid by annexes
-- ד–יא. §43: the tables of annexes ה–ז and ט–יא, for non-academic
-- existing principals, replace annexes י"ד, ט"ו and ט"ז of the base
-- agreement (its §77).
@ref akn:art_41
`chapter ד of 2015 reaches` MEANS `the principal of the institution`

DECLARE `qualification on the 2015 tables` IS ONE OF
    `an academic manager`
    `a senior manager (בכיר)`
    `a certified manager (מוסמך)`
    `an uncertified manager (בלתי מוסמך)`

@ref akn:art_42 akn:art_43
GIVEN q IS A `qualification on the 2015 tables`, `heads an adjacent junior high school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `2015 salary annex`
DECIDE `the annex an existing principal is paid by` q `heads an adjacent junior high school` IS
    CONSIDER q
    WHEN `an academic manager` THEN IF `heads an adjacent junior high school` THEN `annex ח of 2015` ELSE `annex ד of 2015`
    WHEN `a senior manager (בכיר)` THEN IF `heads an adjacent junior high school` THEN `annex ט of 2015` ELSE `annex ה of 2015`
    WHEN `a certified manager (מוסמך)` THEN IF `heads an adjacent junior high school` THEN `annex י of 2015` ELSE `annex ו of 2015`
    WHEN `an uncertified manager (בלתי מוסמך)` THEN IF `heads an adjacent junior high school` THEN `annex יא of 2015` ELSE `annex ז of 2015`

`the base agreement's annexes §43 replaces` MEANS LIST "י\"ד", "ט\"ו", "ט\"ז"

-- §44: placed by their grade on the determining day and the new level the
-- Ministry sets for the institution, after §§45–46.
@ref akn:art_44
GIVEN a IS A `2015 salary annex`, `grade on the determining day` IS A NUMBER, `the new level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `an existing manager's new table pay` a `grade on the determining day` `the new level` IS
    `the 2015 table pay` a `the new level` `grade on the determining day`

#ASSERT `an existing manager's new table pay` (`the annex an existing principal is paid by` `an academic manager` FALSE) 2.5 5 EQUALS JUST 18616

-- §45: the "notional pay for salary protection" G, from E and F. E: the
-- table pay, accumulated complexity supplement, personal percentage and
-- shekel supplements and salary-protection supplement he had in the
-- February salary before the determining day ("his pay on the eve of this
-- agreement"); F: the same he would have had but for the follow-up
-- committee's decision of 12.3.2013 and §14(ו) of the 2013 agreement — an
-- input, those instruments not being encoded.
@ref akn:art_45 akn:art_45/p2 akn:art_45/p3 akn:art_45/p4
@desc A pay §§45 and 55 compare: what it is made of and the level it is computed on.
DECLARE `an existing manager's pay of 2015` HAS
    `the level it is computed on`        IS A NUMBER
    `its table pay`                      IS A NUMBER
    `its role allowances`                IS A NUMBER @desc for a first deputy (§55); nothing for a principal
    `its accumulated complexity supplement` IS A NUMBER
    `its personal supplement`            IS A NUMBER @desc percentage or shekel, at its shekel value
    `its salary-protection supplement`   IS A NUMBER

-- §46: (א) F's level at or below E's: G = E; (ב) F's level one above E's:
-- G = E; (ג) F's level more than one above E's: G is computed on the level
-- one below F's (an input: F's components at that level).
@ref akn:art_46 akn:art_46__para_a akn:art_46__para_b akn:art_46__para_c
GIVEN e IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`, f IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`, `F's pay at the level below F's` IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
DECIDE `G, the notional pay` e f `F's pay at the level below F's` IS
    IF f's `the level it is computed on` AT MOST e's `the level it is computed on` PLUS 1
    THEN e
    ELSE `F's pay at the level below F's`

-- §47: an existing principal whose new table pay (by the tables of §42) is
-- above the table pay in G, and who is paid one or more of these
-- supplements, has them reduced, all or part, by the gap between the two,
-- in this order: (1) the accumulated complexity supplement; (2) the
-- personal percentage or shekel supplement; (3) the offsetting
-- salary-protection supplement. (א) each at its value on G; (ב) a
-- percentage personal supplement by its shekel sum on G; (ג) the
-- accumulated complexity supplement at its updated sum on G by §67 as the
-- completion agreement amended it. §48: only until the whole gap is
-- reduced.
@ref akn:art_47 akn:art_47__para_1 akn:art_47__para_2 akn:art_47__para_3 akn:art_47__para_3__subpara_a akn:art_47__para_3__subpara_b akn:art_47__para_3__subpara_c akn:art_48
GIVEN gap IS A NUMBER, amounts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplements left when a gap is taken from them in order` gap amounts IS
    CONSIDER amounts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `not below zero` (a MINUS gap) FOLLOWED BY `the supplements left when a gap is taken from them in order` (`not below zero` (gap MINUS a)) rest

GIVEN `new table pay` IS A NUMBER, g IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `an existing principal's supplements after the new table` `new table pay` g IS
    `the supplements left when a gap is taken from them in order`
        (`not below zero` (`new table pay` MINUS g's `its table pay`))
        (LIST g's `its accumulated complexity supplement`, g's `its personal supplement`, g's `its salary-protection supplement`)

-- The accumulated complexity supplement's updated sum on G (§47(3)(ג)) is
-- the replaced §67's, imported from the completion agreement.
GIVEN `level value in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated complexity supplement on G` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` IS
    `the accumulated complexity supplement` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value`

-- §49: what is left of the accumulated complexity supplement after §47:
-- (א) the entitlement to it ends; (ב) a shekel supplement of the same sum
-- takes its place, §38ב(ב)(4)–(7) applying with the changes needed; (ג) a
-- rise in the combined salary from the school's level counts for
-- §38ב(ב)(4).
@ref akn:art_49 akn:art_49__para_a akn:art_49__para_b akn:art_49__para_c
GIVEN `what is left of it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement for what is left of the accumulated complexity supplement` `what is left of it` IS
    `what is left of it`

-- §50: what is left of a personal percentage supplement is taken anew as a
-- rate of the new table pay, from the determining day. §51: once the whole
-- gap is reduced, the rest of the supplements are paid at what is left.
-- F-ofek-hadash-principals-2015-a: §§50 and 51 say "after §46" and "the
-- supplements of §46", where §46 sets G and reduces nothing; the reduction
-- and its list are §47's, and the deputies' §§60–61 name their own §57.
-- The reading adopted (convention reading.misprint): §47.
@ref akn:art_50 akn:art_51
GIVEN `what is left of it in shekels` IS A NUMBER, `new table pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the personal supplement's new rate` `what is left of it in shekels` `new table pay` IS
    `what is left of it in shekels` DIVIDED BY `new table pay`

`the section §§50 and 51 name` MEANS 46
`the section that reduces an existing principal's supplements` MEANS 47
`the section §§60 and 61 name` MEANS 57
`the section that reduces an existing deputy's supplements` MEANS 57

`§§50 and 51 point to §46, which reduces nothing` MEANS
        NOT `the section §§50 and 51 name` EQUALS `the section that reduces an existing principal's supplements`
    AND `the section §§60 and 61 name` EQUALS `the section that reduces an existing deputy's supplements`
#ASSERT `§§50 and 51 point to §46, which reduces nothing`

-- §52: an existing principal whose new table pay fell below the table pay
-- in G gets a shekel salary-protection supplement besides it: (א) X, the
-- table pay in G; (ב) Y, the table pay after the determining day; (ג) on
-- placement Z = X − Y where positive; (ד) then taken as a rate of the
-- table pay; (ה) reduced only when the table pay rises from a rise in
-- complexity, by the whole rise, the rate then taken anew; (ו) a rise in
-- grade leaves its shekel value as it is, the rate taken anew; (ז) it
-- counts for pensions, for contributions to a pension provident fund (for
-- one insured in an accrual pension on the determining salary) and for the
-- study fund; (ח) it is the base of no percentage supplement.
@ref akn:art_52 akn:art_52__para_a akn:art_52__para_b akn:art_52__para_c akn:art_52__para_c/p2 akn:art_52__para_c/p3 akn:art_52__para_d akn:art_52__para_e akn:art_52__para_f akn:art_52__para_g akn:art_52__para_h
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z, the 2015 salary-protection supplement` x y IS
    `not below zero` (x MINUS y)

DECLARE `cause of a rise in a manager's table pay` IS ONE OF
    `a rise in the institution's complexity`
    `a rise in grade`
    `another cause of a rise`

GIVEN z IS A NUMBER, `the rise in the table pay` IS A NUMBER, `its cause` IS A `cause of a rise in a manager's table pay`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z after a rise in the table pay` z `the rise in the table pay` `its cause` IS
    IF `its cause` EQUALS `a rise in the institution's complexity`
    THEN `not below zero` (z MINUS `the rise in the table pay`)
    ELSE z

GIVEN z IS A NUMBER, `table pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z's rate of the table pay` z `table pay` IS
    z DIVIDED BY `table pay`

GIVEN p IS A `purpose of a salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Z counts for` p IF
        p EQUALS `pensions`
    OR  p EQUALS `pension-fund contributions for one insured in an accrual pension`
    OR  p EQUALS `study-fund contributions`

-- An academic principal of a level-2 school on the eve, grade ב+ (16,630 at
-- level 2 of annex ד), G's table pay 16,000 and supplements of 300, 400
-- and 500: the gap of 630 takes the 300 and 330 of the 400. Had the school
-- fallen to level 1 (15,838 at ב+), Z = 16,000 − 15,838 = 162; a rise to
-- level 2 later takes the whole of it, a rise in grade nothing.
`an academic principal's G` MEANS
    `an existing manager's pay of 2015` WITH
        `the level it is computed on`        IS 2
        `its table pay`                      IS 16000
        `its role allowances`                IS 0
        `its accumulated complexity supplement` IS 300
        `its personal supplement`            IS 400
        `its salary-protection supplement`   IS 500

#ASSERT `an existing principal's supplements after the new table` 16630 `an academic principal's G` EQUALS LIST 0, 70, 500
#ASSERT `Z, the 2015 salary-protection supplement` 16000 15838 EQUALS 162
#ASSERT `Z after a rise in the table pay` 162 792 `a rise in the institution's complexity` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Z after a rise in the table pay` 162 792 `a rise in grade` EQUALS 162
#ASSERT NOT `Z counts for` `the base of percentage supplements`
#ASSERT `G, the notional pay` `an academic principal's G` `an academic principal's G` `an academic principal's G` EQUALS `an academic principal's G`

§§ `ה. שכר סגני מנהלים קיימים`

-- akn:chp_5 The heading of chapter ה; its definition and articles follow.

