    WHEN `an uncertified manager (בלתי מוסמך)` THEN `annex טו of 2015`

-- §54: placed in the new tables by their grade on the determining day and
-- the new level (`an existing manager's new table pay`). §§55–56: G from E
-- and F as §§45–46, E and F carrying the role allowances too.
@ref akn:art_54 akn:art_55 akn:art_55/p2 akn:art_55/p3 akn:art_56 akn:art_56__para_1 akn:art_56__para_2 akn:art_56__para_3
GIVEN e IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`, f IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`, `F's pay at the level below F's` IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
DECIDE `a deputy's G, the notional pay` e f `F's pay at the level below F's` IS
    `G, the notional pay` e f `F's pay at the level below F's`

-- §57: an existing deputy whose new table pay with the role allowances on
-- it ("AF new") is above the notional table pay with the role allowances
-- on it ("AF notional") has the supplements of (1)–(3) reduced, in that
-- order, by the gap between the two AFs; (א)–(ג) as §47(3). §58: only until
-- the whole AF gap is reduced. §59: what is left of the accumulated
-- complexity supplement becomes a shekel supplement, as §49. §60: what is
-- left of the personal percentage supplement is taken anew on the new
-- table pay.
-- F-ofek-hadash-principals-2015-g: §61 says the rest is paid "after the
-- whole gap between the new table pay and the table pay in the notional
-- pay" is reduced — the table pays' gap, where §§57–58 reduce by the AFs'.
-- The reading adopted (convention precedence.clarification): §61, written
-- "for the avoidance of doubt", clarifies §§57–58 and the AF gap governs.
@ref akn:art_57 akn:art_57__para_1 akn:art_57__para_2 akn:art_57__para_3 akn:art_57__para_3__subpara_a akn:art_57__para_3__subpara_b akn:art_57__para_3__subpara_c akn:art_58 akn:art_59 akn:art_59__para_a akn:art_59__para_b akn:art_59__para_c akn:art_60 akn:art_61
GIVEN `table pay` IS A NUMBER, `rate of the role allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `AF, table pay with its role allowances` `table pay` `rate of the role allowances` IS
    `table pay` TIMES (1 PLUS `rate of the role allowances`)

GIVEN `new table pay` IS A NUMBER, `rate of the role allowances` IS A NUMBER, g IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the AF gap` `new table pay` `rate of the role allowances` g IS
    `not below zero` (`AF, table pay with its role allowances` `new table pay` `rate of the role allowances` MINUS `AF, table pay with its role allowances` (g's `its table pay`) `rate of the role allowances`)

GIVEN `new table pay` IS A NUMBER, `rate of the role allowances` IS A NUMBER, g IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `an existing deputy's supplements after the new table` `new table pay` `rate of the role allowances` g IS
    `the supplements left when a gap is taken from them in order`
        (`the AF gap` `new table pay` `rate of the role allowances` g)
        (LIST g's `its accumulated complexity supplement`, g's `its personal supplement`, g's `its salary-protection supplement`)

GIVEN `new table pay` IS A NUMBER, g IS AN `an existing manager's pay of 2015`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the table-pay gap §61 names` `new table pay` g IS
    `not below zero` (`new table pay` MINUS g's `its table pay`)

-- A deputy with role allowances of 10%, G's table pay 12,000, new 12,500:
-- the AFs part by 550, the table pays by 500.
`an academic deputy's G` MEANS
    `an existing manager's pay of 2015` WITH
        `the level it is computed on`        IS 4
        `its table pay`                      IS 12000
        `its role allowances`                IS 1200
        `its accumulated complexity supplement` IS 300
        `its personal supplement`            IS 400
        `its salary-protection supplement`   IS 0

`§61's gap is not the gap §§57–58 reduce by` MEANS
        `the AF gap` 12500 (10%) `an academic deputy's G` EQUALS 550
    AND `the table-pay gap §61 names` 12500 `an academic deputy's G` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `§61's gap is not the gap §§57–58 reduce by`
#ASSERT `an existing deputy's supplements after the new table` 12500 (10%) `an academic deputy's G` EQUALS LIST 0, 150, 0

-- §62: an existing deputy whose new table pay fell below the table pay in
-- G gets Z besides it: X the table pay in G with its role allowances, Y
-- the table pay after the determining day with its role allowances; (1)
-- Z = X − Y where positive; (2) taken as a rate of the table pay; (3)
-- reduced at a rise from a change of complexity, by the whole rise, its
-- shekel value kept at a rise in grade; (4) counts for pensions, the
-- pension provident fund and the study fund; (5) the base of no percentage
-- supplement — §52's rules, imported above.
@ref akn:art_62 akn:art_62/p2 akn:art_62/p3 akn:art_62__para_1 akn:art_62__para_1/p2 akn:art_62__para_1/p3 akn:art_62__para_2 akn:art_62__para_3 akn:art_62__para_4 akn:art_62__para_5
GIVEN `X, G's table pay with role allowances` IS A NUMBER, `Y, the new table pay with role allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a deputy's Z of 2015` `X, G's table pay with role allowances` `Y, the new table pay with role allowances` IS
    `Z, the 2015 salary-protection supplement` `X, G's table pay with role allowances` `Y, the new table pay with role allowances`

#ASSERT `a deputy's Z of 2015` 13200 13000 EQUALS 200

§§ `ו. שעות הוראה פרונטאלית למנהלים ולסגני מנהלים ראשונים`

-- akn:chp_6 The heading of chapter ו; its articles follow.

-- §63: in force from 1.9.2015; to the end of תשע"ה principals and first
-- deputies teach the frontal hours they owed on the eve of signing (an
-- input: the base agreement's §§64 and 90 as they stood, by the level the
-- school had then).
@ref akn:art_63
`the 2015 frontal hours start` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2015

-- §64: in place of §64's table for principals: levels 1–8 teach 9, 9, 9,
-- 8, 8, 7, 7 and 6 weekly frontal hours.
@ref akn:art_64
GIVEN level IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principal's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` level IS
    BRANCH IF level AT MOST 3 THEN 9
           IF level AT MOST 5 THEN 8
           IF level AT MOST 7 THEN 7
           OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN level IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, `owed on the eve of signing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principal's frontal hours on` level d `owed on the eve of signing` IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the 2015 frontal hours start`
    THEN `a principal's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` level
    ELSE `owed on the eve of signing`

#ASSERT map `a principal's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` (range 1 8) EQUALS LIST 9, 9, 9, 8, 8, 7, 7, 6
-- Levels 1–4 lose nothing against §64's 9, 8, 7, 6.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD `a principal's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` l AT LEAST `a principal's frontal teaching hours` l) (range 1 4)

-- §65: in place of §90(ב)'s tables for first deputies: in a primary school
-- (and a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils) 21, 21, 21, 21, 20,
-- 20, 19, 18; in a junior high school (and one serving junior high pupils)
-- 11 at levels 1–6 and 9 at 7–8; in a multi-stage special-education school
-- none at 1–2 ("-") and 15, 15, 14, 14, 13, 13 at 3–8; on a farm or marine
-- centre serving both, 16, 16, 16, 16, 15, 15, 14, 13. A level a table
-- marks "-" has no figure (convention thresholds.missing-row).
-- F-ofek-hadash-principals-2015-f: §70 voids §90(ב) "as amended" from this
-- agreement's start, the §90(ב) whose tables §65 replaces. The reading
-- adopted is the lawyer's pick (convention instruments.void-as-amended,
-- MMS-320): the voiding takes the earlier wording; §65's tables are §90(ב)
-- from §63's 1.9.2015.
@ref akn:art_65
DECLARE `a first deputy's institution under §65` IS ONE OF
    `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils`
    `a junior high school, or a farm or marine centre serving junior high pupils`
    `a multi-stage special-education school`
    `a farm or marine centre serving both primary and junior high pupils`

GIVEN k IS A `a first deputy's institution under §65`, level IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a first deputy's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` k level IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils` THEN
        JUST (BRANCH IF level AT MOST 4 THEN 21
                     IF level AT MOST 6 THEN 20
                     IF level EQUALS 7 THEN 19
                     OTHERWISE 18)
    WHEN `a junior high school, or a farm or marine centre serving junior high pupils` THEN
        JUST (IF level AT MOST 6 THEN 11 ELSE 9)
    WHEN `a multi-stage special-education school` THEN
        IF level AT MOST 2 THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (BRANCH IF level AT MOST 4 THEN 15
                          IF level AT MOST 6 THEN 14
                          OTHERWISE 13)
    WHEN `a farm or marine centre serving both primary and junior high pupils` THEN
        JUST (BRANCH IF level AT MOST 4 THEN 16
                     IF level AT MOST 6 THEN 15
                     IF level EQUALS 7 THEN 14
                     OTHERWISE 13)

GIVEN k IS A `a first deputy's institution under §65`
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the §65 table for` k IS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD `a first deputy's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` k l) (range 1 8)

#ASSERT `the §65 table for` `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils` EQUALS LIST JUST 21, JUST 21, JUST 21, JUST 21, JUST 20, JUST 20, JUST 19, JUST 18
#ASSERT `the §65 table for` `a junior high school, or a farm or marine centre serving junior high pupils` EQUALS LIST JUST 11, JUST 11, JUST 11, JUST 11, JUST 11, JUST 11, JUST 9, JUST 9
#ASSERT `the §65 table for` `a multi-stage special-education school` EQUALS LIST NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST 15, JUST 15, JUST 14, JUST 14, JUST 13, JUST 13
#ASSERT `the §65 table for` `a farm or marine centre serving both primary and junior high pupils` EQUALS LIST JUST 16, JUST 16, JUST 16, JUST 16, JUST 15, JUST 15, JUST 14, JUST 13
-- At level 1 a primary deputy teaches 21 as under §90(ב).
#ASSERT `a first deputy's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils` 1 EQUALS JUST (`a first deputy's frontal hours` `a primary school` 1)

`the sections §65 rewrites` MEANS LIST "90(ב)"

-- F-ofek-hadash-principals-2015-c: a first deputy at a level-1 primary
-- school teaches 21 frontal hours by §65, and annexes ג and יב–טו print no
-- level 1: the tables open at level 2. No pay is given him here
-- (convention thresholds.missing-row).
`a first deputy at level 1 has frontal hours and no pay row` MEANS
        `a first deputy's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils` 1 EQUALS JUST 21
    AND `the 2015 table pay` `annex ג of 2015` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the 2015 table pay` `annex יב of 2015` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the 2015 table pay` `annex א of 2015` 1 1 EQUALS JUST 13953
#ASSERT `a first deputy at level 1 has frontal hours and no pay row`

§§ `ז. שינוי בשכר המנהל ושכרו של סגן מנהל כתוצאה משינוי רמת המורכבות`

-- akn:chp_7 The heading of chapter ז; its articles follow.

-- §66: from this agreement's start, §67 of the base agreement, as the
-- completion agreement amended it, is void.
@ref akn:art_66
`the sections §66 voids` MEANS LIST "67"

-- §67: on a rise or fall in the school's level, the principal or deputy
-- gets the table pay set for the new level of that school year.
@ref akn:art_67
GIVEN a IS A `2015 salary annex`, `the year's level` IS A NUMBER, `the grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the table pay after a change of level` a `the year's level` `the grade` IS
    `the 2015 table pay` a `the year's level` `the grade`

-- §68(א): notwithstanding §67, a principal who headed a school for at least
-- eight consecutive years on the eve of the change gets each year the
-- higher of (1) the pay on the school's level that year and (2) the pay on
-- the mean of the levels of the school or schools he headed in the last
-- four years, rounded to the nearest level (a fraction from .0 to below .5
-- down, from .5 up — the text's own rounding, convention rounding.half's).
-- (ב): for תשע"ה–תשע"ז the Ministry's procedure on complexity levels sets
-- how that mean is computed (an input). §69: the same for first deputies
-- of eight consecutive years, with the changes needed.
@ref akn:art_68 akn:art_68__para_a akn:art_68__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_68__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_68__para_b akn:art_69
GIVEN `levels in the last four years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the mean level of the last four years, rounded` `levels in the last four years` IS
    `to the nearest whole` (sum `levels in the last four years` DIVIDED BY count `levels in the last four years`)

GIVEN `the year opens in` IS A NUMBER
      `levels in the last four years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the mean the Ministry's procedure sets` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the mean level §68 uses` `the year opens in` `levels in the last four years` `the mean the Ministry's procedure sets` IS
    IF `the year opens in` AT LEAST 2014 AND `the year opens in` AT MOST 2016
    THEN fromMaybe (`the mean level of the last four years, rounded` `levels in the last four years`) `the mean the Ministry's procedure sets`
    ELSE `the mean level of the last four years, rounded` `levels in the last four years`

GIVEN a IS A `2015 salary annex`, `the grade` IS A NUMBER, `the year's level` IS A NUMBER, `the mean level` IS A NUMBER, `consecutive years in the post on the eve of the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the table pay of a manager of eight years after a change of level` a `the grade` `the year's level` `the mean level` `consecutive years in the post on the eve of the change` IS
    IF `consecutive years in the post on the eve of the change` AT LEAST 8
    THEN CONSIDER `the 2015 table pay` a `the year's level` `the grade`
         WHEN JUST p THEN CONSIDER `the 2015 table pay` a `the mean level` `the grade`
                          WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (max p q)
                          WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST p
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `the 2015 table pay` a `the year's level` `the grade`

#ASSERT `the mean level of the last four years, rounded` (LIST 5, 5, 4, 4) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the mean level of the last four years, rounded` (LIST 5, 4, 4, 4) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the mean level §68 uses` 2015 (LIST 5, 5, 4, 4) (JUST 4) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the mean level §68 uses` 2017 (LIST 5, 5, 4, 4) (JUST 4) EQUALS 5
-- A principal of nine years whose school falls from 5 to 4 keeps level 5's pay.
#ASSERT `the table pay of a manager of eight years after a change of level` `annex ד of 2015` 2 4 5 9 EQUALS JUST 17836
#ASSERT `the table pay of a manager of eight years after a change of level` `annex ד of 2015` 2 4 5 7 EQUALS JUST 17233

-- §70: from this agreement's start, §§65, 66, 67, 90(ב) and 92–93 of the
-- base agreement, as §§43, 44, 45, 46, 54, 57 and 59 of the completion
-- agreement amended them, are void. Their rules stay in their modules for
-- the time before 1.3.2014.
@ref akn:art_70
`the sections §70 voids` MEANS LIST "65", "66", "67", "90(ב)", "92", "93"

GIVEN `the section` IS A STRING, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a base-agreement section the 2015 principals' agreement voids is in force on` `the section` d IF
    (NOT elem `the section` `the sections §70 voids`) OR NOT d `is on or after` `the 2015 principals' changes apply from`

#ASSERT NOT `a base-agreement section the 2015 principals' agreement voids is in force on` "67" `the 2015 principals' changes apply from`
#ASSERT `a base-agreement section the 2015 principals' agreement voids is in force on` "67" (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2014)

`§70 voids the §90(ב) that §65 rewrites` MEANS
    elem "90(ב)" `the sections §70 voids` AND elem "90(ב)" `the sections §65 rewrites`
#ASSERT `§70 voids the §90(ב) that §65 rewrites`

-- The lawyer's pick (MMS-320): the §65 tables stand from 1.9.2015 though
-- §70 voids §90(ב).
GIVEN level IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, `owed on the eve of signing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a primary first deputy's frontal hours on` level d `owed on the eve of signing` IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the 2015 frontal hours start`
    THEN `a first deputy's frontal hours from 1.9.2015` `a primary school, or a farm or marine centre serving primary pupils` level
    ELSE JUST `owed on the eve of signing`

#ASSERT `a primary first deputy's frontal hours on` 8 `the 2015 frontal hours start` 20 EQUALS JUST 18

§§ `ז. מיצוי תביעות`

-- akn:chp_8 The heading of the chapter on exhaustion of claims (printed ז again); its paragraphs follow.

-- ¶1: the agreement exhausts the parties' claims on what it settles for
-- the time to 30.6.2015, and no further negotiation on economic demands
-- for its period. ¶2: every claim under §14 of the 2013 agreement, its
-- cost frame included, is exhausted, and not negotiated further.
@ref akn:chp_8/p1 akn:chp_8/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2015 principals' agreement action`
DECIDE `the 2015 principals' agreement exhausts the claims` IS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands for the agreement's period`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands for the agreement's period`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `raise a further claim under §14 of the 2013 agreement`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `raise a further claim under §14 of the 2013 agreement`)

§§ `ח. שקט תעשייתי`

-- akn:chp_9 The heading of chapter ח; its paragraph follows.

-- While it is in force no party, nor any unit of it, strikes or locks out,
-- wholly or partly, or otherwise disrupts work in an organised way, over a
-- matter it settles; the industrial peace of the 2013 agreement stands.
@ref akn:chp_9/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2015 principals' agreement action`
DECIDE `the 2015 principals' industrial peace` IS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or otherwise disrupt work over a matter the agreement settles`
     WITHIN DATE_SERIAL `the 2015 principals' agreement ends` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the signing of the 2015 principals' agreement`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or otherwise disrupt work over a matter the agreement settles`
     WITHIN DATE_SERIAL `the 2015 principals' agreement ends` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the signing of the 2015 principals' agreement`)

§§ `ט. יישוב חילוקי דעות`

-- akn:chp_10 The heading of chapter ט; its paragraph follows.

-- A parity follow-up committee of the parties follows the agreement's
-- carrying out and decides disputes over its application or reading; its
-- decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:chp_10/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2015 principals' agreement action`
DECIDE `the 2015 follow-up committee decides a dispute` IS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `decide a dispute over the agreement's application or reading`

`the 2015 follow-up committee's decisions are final and binding` MEANS TRUE

